cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software

title: "gliostitch: reproducible cohort selection over public glioma MRI datasets"
abstract: >-
  gliostitch assembles a single manifest of facts over several public glioma MRI
  datasets — BraTS-2020, UCSF-PDGM, UPENN-GBM and RHUH-GBM — reconciling their
  directory layouts, clinical vocabularies and identifier formats, and annotating
  patients that appear in more than one cohort. Study eligibility is expressed
  separately as a declarative, versioned definition applied at load time, so the
  manifest is unchanged by the research question asked of it. Every excluded
  session is attributed to the criterion that removed it, making the cohort table
  derivable rather than asserted.

